1. the two defaults
   str(Plain()) starts with "<__main__.Plain object at 0x" True
   repr(Plain()) == str(Plain())            True
   repr(Point(1, 2)) mentions x             True
   vars(Point(1, 2))                        {'x': 1, 'y': 2}
2. __str__ never defines __repr__; __repr__ does define str
   str(OnlyStr())                           only __str__
   repr(OnlyStr()) is still the default     True
   repr(OnlyRepr())                         <OnlyRepr>
   str(OnlyRepr())  (falls back to __repr__) <OnlyRepr>
3. who calls which
   print(obj)                               str of 3
   p(obj)                                   <Both 3>
   f"{obj}"                                 str of 3
   "%s / %r" % (obj, obj)                   str of 3 / <Both 3>
   str(obj)                                 str of 3
   f"{obj!s}"                               str of 3
   f"{obj!r}"                               <Both 3>
4. containers repr their elements, even in str
   str([obj])                               [<Both 3>]
   repr([obj])                              [<Both 3>]
   str({"k": obj})                          {'k': <Both 3>}
   f"{[obj]}"                               [<Both 3>]
   print([obj])                             [<Both 3>]
5. print returns None; the p helper returns its argument
   p(obj) prints: <Both 3>
     ...and returns obj itself              True
   p(1, 2) prints two lines:
1
2
     ...and returns                         [1, 2]
   p() returns                              None
   print("one") prints: one
     ...and returns                         None
6. None
   print(None) writes                       'None\n'
   p(None) writes                           'None\n'
   print(None, end='') writes               'None'
   repr(f"{None}")                          'None'
   repr(str(None))                          'None'
   repr(None)                               None
   str([None])                              [None]
7. strings; no symbol, so an Enum member
   str("str")                               str
   repr("str")                              'str'
   repr("tab\there")                        'tab\there'
   repr("\N{LATIN SMALL LETTER E WITH ACUTE}") 'é'
   str(Sym.sym)                             Sym.sym
   repr(Sym.sym)                            <Sym.sym: 1>
8. stdlib classes define both
   repr(S(1, 2))                            S(x=1, y=2)
   str(S(1, 2)) == repr(S(1, 2))            True
   repr(NT(1))                              NT(a=1)
   str(RuntimeError("boom"))                boom
   repr(RuntimeError("boom"))               RuntimeError('boom')
   str(1e20)                                1e+20
   repr(range(1, 4))                        range(1, 4)
9. pprint wraps a nested structure at a width
{'name': 'widget',
 'parts': [{'id': 1,
            'tags': ['alpha',
                     'beta',
                     'gamma']},
           {'id': 2,
            'tags': ['alpha',
                     'beta',
                     'gamma']},
           {'id': 3,
            'tags': ['alpha',
                     'beta',
                     'gamma']}]}
   pprint.pformat(obj) == repr(obj)         True
10. where they live
   Plain.__str__ is object.__str__          True
   Plain.__repr__ is object.__repr__        True
   hasattr(builtins, 'print')               True
   hasattr(object, '__repr__')              True
